The LIFECYCLE is the key differentiator:

```java
// ═══ AGGREGATION: Branch HAS Employees — independent lifecycle ═══
public class Branch {
    private String branchCode;
    private List<Employee> employees = new ArrayList<>();

    // Branch does NOT create employees — they are ADDED from outside
    public void addEmployee(Employee emp) { employees.add(emp); }
    public void removeEmployee(Employee emp) { employees.remove(emp); }

    // When branch is closed: employees SURVIVE
    public List<Employee> close() {
        List<Employee> surviving = new ArrayList<>(employees);
        employees.clear();
        return surviving;  // employees returned — they LIVE ON
    }
}

// Employee exists independently:
Employee rajesh = new Employee("E001", "Rajesh Kumar");  // created OUTSIDE Branch
Branch mumbai = new Branch("MUM001");
mumbai.addEmployee(rajesh);  // added to branch
mumbai.close();              // branch closed
// rajesh still exists! Can join another branch.
```

