// ═══ COMPOSITION: Loan OWNS EMIs — bound lifecycle ═══
public class Loan {
    private String loanId;
    private BigDecimal principal;
    private final List<EMI> emis = new ArrayList<>();  // OWNED by Loan

    public Loan(String loanId, BigDecimal principal, int tenureMonths, BigDecimal rate) {
        this.loanId = loanId;
        this.principal = principal;
        // Loan CREATES EMIs — they are born with the loan
        generateEMIs(tenureMonths, rate);
    }

    private void generateEMIs(int months, BigDecimal rate) {
        BigDecimal emiAmount = calculateEMI(principal, rate, months);
        for (int i = 1; i <= months; i++) {
            emis.add(new EMI(loanId + "-EMI-" + i, i, emiAmount));
            // EMI created BY the Loan — has no meaning without this Loan
        }
    }

    // When loan is closed: EMIs are DESTROYED
    public void close() {
        emis.clear();  // EMIs die with the loan — composition!
        // In JPA: cascade = ALL + orphanRemoval = true
        // DELETE FROM emis WHERE loan_id = 'LOAN-001'
    }

    public List<EMI> getEmis() { return List.copyOf(emis); }
}

// EMI cannot exist alone:
// new EMI("EMI-1", 1, amount);  ← meaningless without a Loan!
// Which loan? What principal? What tenure? EMI depends on Loan for context.
```

JPA mapping difference:

```java
// ═══ AGGREGATION in JPA: NO cascade delete ═══
@Entity
public class Branch {
    @Id private String branchCode;

    @ManyToMany  // or @OneToMany without cascade
    private List<Employee> employees;
    // Deleting Branch does NOT delete Employees!
    // Employee rows survive in the database.
}

// ═══ COMPOSITION in JPA: cascade ALL + orphanRemoval ═══
@Entity
public class Loan {
    @Id private String loanId;

    @OneToMany(mappedBy = "loan", cascade = CascadeType.ALL, orphanRemoval = true)
    private List<EMI> emis;
    // Deleting Loan ALSO deletes all its EMIs!
    // Removing EMI from list → orphanRemoval deletes the DB row.
}
```

WHEN to use each:

```java
// AGGREGATION — when:
// - Child has independent lifecycle (Employee exists without Branch)
// - Child can belong to MULTIPLE parents (Employee in Branch AND in Project)
// - Child is created OUTSIDE the parent (injected, added from external source)
// - Deleting parent should NOT delete children

// COMPOSITION — when:
// - Child has NO meaning without parent (EMI without Loan = meaningless)
// - Child is created BY the parent (Loan generates its EMIs)
// - Child belongs to EXACTLY ONE parent (EMI belongs to one Loan)
// - Deleting parent MUST delete children (cascade + orphanRemoval)
```

