  class Account {                     // COMPOSITION owner
     private final List<Transaction> txns = new ArrayList<>();
     void post(BigDecimal amt){
        txns.add(new Transaction(amt, Instant.now())); // created INSIDE
     }
     // when Account is GC'd, its txns are unreachable too → die together
  }

  class Bank {                        // AGGREGATION owner
     private final List<Customer> customers;            // passed IN
     Bank(List<Customer> c){ this.customers = c; }      // shared refs
     // Customer objects outlive Bank — created & owned ELSEWHERE
  }

  Composition  ◆  : part has NO independent existence (Account→Transaction)
  Aggregation  ◇  : part lives on its own     (Bank→Customer)

  Test: "If I delete the whole, should the part also die?"
        yes → composition   |   no → aggregation

  SOLID: both favor HAS-A over inheritance (loose coupling).
```
